---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { pick } from '../data/faq';
---
<Guide
  page="arr"
  lede="Yes. Cupola is a free, open-source app for Radarr, Sonarr, Lidarr and Readarr on iPhone, Android and Mac. Your library, calendar, queue and releases, on your phone."
  screen="title"
  services={['radarr', 'sonarr', 'lidarr', 'readarr', 'bazarr', 'prowlarr']}
  questions={pick('arrApp', 'account', 'away', 'certs', 'free')}
  related={['seerr', 'downloads', 'install']}
>
  <h2>What you can do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Browse your library.</strong> Movies, series, artists and authors, and where each one stands.</li>
    <li><strong>See what is coming.</strong> A calendar of episodes and movies, with cinema, digital and disc dates.</li>
    <li><strong>Search your way.</strong> Let Radarr or Sonarr pick a release, or choose one yourself.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix what got stuck.</strong> Manual import for misnamed files, and a search for anything wanted.</li>
    <li><strong>Change your mind.</strong> Toggle monitoring, switch the quality profile, or delete, with or without the files.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Seasons, artists and authors</h2>
  <p>Series open on their seasons and episodes, each with its own search. Artists and authors get a page with every album or book. Bazarr and Prowlarr sit alongside.</p>

  <h2>More than one of each</h2>
  <p>Run two Radarrs, one for 4K? Add both. Cupola shows them together or one at a time.</p>

  <h2>From a poster to your server</h2>
  <p>With Seerr connected, any title opens on one page that shows where it stands everywhere. Add it or request it in one tap, then follow the download in Activity.</p>

  <h2>What you need</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The address and API key of each instance. The key is under <strong>Settings › General</strong> in its web interface.</li>
    <li>A way to reach it: your home network, a VPN or a reverse proxy.</li>
    <li>Nothing to install on the server, and no Cupola account.</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>
